{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "How both SDKs read what the cloud service returns beyond spans (rules-engine#89): a result's `cloud` block, which 429 is final, a batch's cost fields, and the account and job endpoints an API key may call. Wire payloads are the gateway's JSON (euredact-inference f2ea1d9); expectations use the Python field names, and the TypeScript test compares after converting its camelCase names. A field of the wrong type reads as null; nothing here may fail a request. `usage` parsing has its own file, cloud_usage.json. A 402 is the Budget and extra volume spent (rules-engine#145): InsufficientCreditsError, never retried, its numbers read from `detail` (absent or malformed -> null). `account.credits*` include the Budget and extra-volume breakdown (rules-engine#146), null when the service sends none.",
